A multi-module repository (two independent modules, no go.work) where the only
vulnerability lives in the CHILD module at sub/. The root module example.com/foo
is benign; the child module example.com/foo/sub uses net/http and is affected by
GO-2024-2687 / CVE-2023-45288 (HTTP/2 CONTINUATION flood), fixed in go1.21.9. The
desired remediation is sub/go.mod `go 1.21.0` -> `go 1.21.9`.

EXPECTED: FAIL.

GAP: the vulncheck bot script runs only at the repo root, and `go ... ./...` does
not descend into the separate nested module under sub/, so the child's net/http
vulnerability is never even scanned; the root scan reports no called vulns and the
pipeline is empty, so `go mod tidy` changes nothing. Two further gaps compound this:
(1) the bot cannot remediate standard-library vulnerabilities at all -- it only
knows how to `go get` module versions, while stdlib fixes come from the go
directive/toolchain; and (2) under GOTOOLCHAIN=local with an installed go1.26,
govulncheck evaluates the stdlib against the running toolchain, so it never reports
the go1.21.9 fix. Even scanning the child directly, stdlib fix lines read like
`Fixed in: go1.21.9` (no `@`) so the awk skips them; the only `@`-bearing lines are
newer CVEs such as `crypto/tls@go1.26.5`, and `go get crypto/tls@go1.26.5` errors
("can't request explicit version of standard library package"). The script produces
an EMPTY diff while want_diff bumps the child go directive, so the case fails.
-- go.mod --
module example.com/foo

go 1.22.0
-- main.go --
package main

import "fmt"

// main prints a greeting. Nothing here touches the standard-library HTTP/2
// stack, so the root module has no vulnerabilities of its own.
func main() {
	fmt.Println("hello from example.com/foo")
}
-- sub/go.mod --
module example.com/foo/sub

go 1.21.0
-- sub/server.go --
package sub

import "net/http"

// net/http is the vulnerable stdlib package (GO-2024-2687).
func Serve() (*http.Response, error) {
	return http.Get("http://example.com/")
}
-- want_diff.txt --
diff --git a/sub/go.mod b/sub/go.mod
index 39cf66d..655fb81 100644
--- a/sub/go.mod
+++ b/sub/go.mod
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
 module example.com/foo/sub
 
-go 1.21.0
+go 1.21.9
